For external validation, we utilized an independent cohort from the Alzheimer’s Disease Neuroimaging Initiative (ADNI), comprising 290 participants (160 CU, 118 MCI, and 12 dementia) with a median follow-up of 5.5 years (95% CI 5.1–6.0 years) (Table 1). Adjusted survival curves showed consistent patterns of worsening prognosis across stages for very mild and mild dementia outcomes, although moderate dementia differentiation was less distinct due to limited event occurrences in lower stages (Fig. 5a, b). Also, stages III, IVA, and IVB were excluded from analysis due to small sample sizes (N
